WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:01.863
- [Mark] All right.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.780
- How long are you here for you here for,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.613
you here for typically?

00:00:07.613 --> 00:00:09.850
- [Mark] Typically like
today I'm just here for you.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:10.683
- Yeah.

00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:11.570
- [Mark] But typically...

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.640
Typically I'm here from about
10:30 or 11 in the morning

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.551
until three or four or five.

00:00:19.551 --> 00:00:20.384
- Okay.

00:00:20.384 --> 00:00:22.047
- [Mark] And it kind
of depends on who's...

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.680
some days I come down here
and it's magic and it's like,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.880
oh my God that was a great
one. That was a great one.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.840
- Yeah, 'cause you get back to back

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.141
- [Mark] And other days I come down here,

00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:30.710
and it's like that was a whole day wasted

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.840
with nothing I'm going to use.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.327
I just throw out everything I sat through.

00:00:34.327 --> 00:00:36.420
- And do you make money off YouTube?

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.720
- [Mark] Well, I just monetized
just a couple weeks ago

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.370
and I haven't made a penny yet,

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.270
but I'd really like to travel for this.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.103
- Yeah.

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:45.210
- [Mark] That's my number one goal.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.190
- Like in America or?

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.230
- [Mark] Just America I think,

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.698
'cause to travel all over the world would,

00:00:50.698 --> 00:00:52.390
it gets so expensive and time consuming

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.353
that it would be hard
to do this. I'm one guy.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.186
- Yeah.

00:00:55.186 --> 00:00:56.019
- [Mark] You see what my operation--

00:00:56.019 --> 00:00:56.852
- Yeah.

00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:57.787
- [Mark] People will make
comments on YouTube and be like,

00:00:57.787 --> 00:00:58.832
"tell your team to do this."

00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:00.022
What fucking team?

00:01:00.022 --> 00:01:00.855
(Hayden laughs)

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:01.940
You're looking at my team.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.000
- The teams the guys that have the shirt.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.350
- [Mark] Yeah, those guys
just want money from me,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.340
so that's my team, so there is no team,

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.910
but if I started making money on YouTube

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:09.810
I would pay an editor.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.550
I would pay somebody to help
me with the donation campaigns,

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:16.670
which is really ball, it's
the hardest part of what I do.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.852
That's why I don't do a lot of them,

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:18.810
- Yeah.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.030
- [Mark] Because every time
I do one, I always regret it.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.670
Every day that it's
active, except for Jerry.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:24.503
- Yeah.

00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:26.460
- [Mark] What I'm doing for
Jerry right now. He's cool.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.570
I could do a donation campaign

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:28.850
for guys like Jerry all day long.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.683
- His name is Jerry? Jerry?

00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:30.650
- [Mark] That's the guy
that got shot in the face.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.600
- Oh, Jerry! I've seen him,
I think I've seen him once.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.330
Yeah, I watched that one
too, that guy's amazing.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.067
- [Mark] Yeah, he's an amazing
dude, and he's very likable.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.610
- So at the Dream Center we have like

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:44.900
short term missioners come, so
people that come do a weekly,

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.360
I've led like teams of 50 going home,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.550
and I'm like don't come
down here thinking that,

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.113
like it's all about them.

00:01:51.113 --> 00:01:53.017
Like people sometimes
will teach you things,

00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:55.857
and like tell you things where
you walk away and you're like

00:01:55.857 --> 00:01:58.483
"wow, I think that person
did more for me than what,

00:01:58.483 --> 00:01:59.600
like guys like Jerry.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.470
You can see he's one of those guys,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.997
like with the wizard in me,
he's just like, you know.

00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:03.350
You're like, "wow."

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.810
- [Mark] Yeah, you think
you're going to save them.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.210
- Yeah. No, he ends up saving
you, and you're like wow.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.800
Yeah, definitely.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.460
- [Mark] Yeah, no it's
interesting how all these dynamics

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.143
of human interaction are so interesting.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.830
All right so, Hayden,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.760
so you work at a place
called The Dream Center?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.593
- [Hayden] Yes.

00:02:19.593 --> 00:02:20.480
- [Mark] So you're from Australia?

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.760
- [Hayden] From Australia, Sydney, yeah.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:22.670
- [Mark] And you're fairly new here.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.900
You've been here how long?

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.650
- 15 months about, yeah,
so January of 2018.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.730
- [Mark] And you're working
primarily with people

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:33.090
from Skid Row that are
fighting addiction issues?

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.540
- Yes, I've been coming to Skid Row,

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.150
like a couple of times a week
for over a year now, yeah.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.050
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:39.980
- Yeah.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.623
- [Mark] And tell me, like,

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.060
you've seen some of the
videos on my channel.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:45.893
- Yeah.

00:02:45.893 --> 00:02:47.360
- [Mark] You contacted me
and that's why we're here,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.810
but what have you learned

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.590
from your time with all these people?

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.450
- What have I learned?

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.513
- [Mark] I mean what is the
most misunderstood thing?

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.840
- That they're not people, so like,

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.070
these are people who were
babies were children,

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.080
who had a, you know, a
childhood, who had dreams,

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:10.080
who had goals and stuff and, you know,

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.390
give or take with what's
happened in their life,

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:14.320
they've had a few bad, you know,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.600
some people have been
dealt a rougher, you know,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.990
hand of cards, I guess you'd say,

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.520
on what their life has been themed,

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.240
but I think they're just,
yeah, they're people.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.810
They grew up, you know,
people played sport,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.500
they went to high school,
they did things like that,

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.600
so I think the thing is to forget,

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.980
because of the condition they can get in

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.490
or where they're at when you see them,

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.850
you forget that, hey,
this person wasn't here.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.520
He hasn't been here his whole life.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.280
So I think one thing is just
trying to find their story,

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.330
and whether they've been here
for one month or 10 years.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.370
Find out what do you actually
want to do with your life

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.870
and how can we help them?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.400
Or how are they going to get
out of here? Which I think is,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.950
that's the big question
with the housing in LA

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.063
and the government and how it
all kind of works with that.

00:03:58.063 --> 00:03:59.500
- [Mark] Have you seen successful stories

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.510
where people have--

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.060
- I've had people that I've prayed for

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.015
who have gotten housing,

00:04:04.015 --> 00:04:07.510
and then with not a lot
of people having phones,

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.240
I haven't heard from
them, but I've just heard,

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.100
Hey, they left they got out of here

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.530
and they got housing and things like that.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:16.050
So there are, as far
as successful stories,

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.540
I haven't been in touch with many,

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.560
because once they get out of here,

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.779
they kind of just disappear.

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:21.612
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:21.612 --> 00:04:24.770
- I've had a few like stray
phone calls from odd numbers,

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.320
which is people saying
that they got out of there

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.759
and they're in different
areas and stuff, but...

00:04:28.759 --> 00:04:29.592
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:29.592 --> 00:04:31.123
- There are, yeah, there
are success stories,

00:04:31.123 --> 00:04:34.790
like it's not a lot.
It's not always all bad.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.430
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.910
So what do you guys do?
You come down here and...

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:43.491
- Yeah, so we come down
Tuesday, Thursday, Friday night,

00:04:43.491 --> 00:04:45.890
Saturday, and then Sunday,

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.520
and sometimes Wednesday, Friday mornings,

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.010
depending on how many people we have.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:50.967
- [Mark] And what do you guys do?

00:04:50.967 --> 00:04:52.710
- Basically The Dream Center is not,

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.060
we're not here to feed as
much as we're here to, like,

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.530
have conversations with these people

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.120
and with us being a
faith-based organization,

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.230
we're trying to help
people get out of here

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.063
and come to The Dream Center.

00:05:01.063 --> 00:05:05.689
I think right now we have a
hundred and... might be 150.

00:05:05.689 --> 00:05:07.290
We can house up to 150 men

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.520
in the men's discipleship program.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.670
And in the women's one, I
think we can house up to

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.190
I'd say 40 or 50, something like that.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.730
I'm not sure on the numbers,

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.060
but we're trying to get people

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.110
into the program that we have.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.805
So the program we have

00:05:20.805 --> 00:05:22.880
is a year long life recovery program,

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.786
so they come in, all their food,

00:05:25.786 --> 00:05:28.120
clothing, you know, taken care of.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.180
It's a residential live-in
program, so it's not a shelter.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.330
It's not they come in, they sleep,

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.650
and then they can leave during the day.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.370
They're there, they have a schedule.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.220
- [Mark] And that's kind
of, that's part of the--

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.053
- Yeah.

00:05:38.053 --> 00:05:38.906
- [Mark] It needs to be that way.

00:05:38.906 --> 00:05:39.739
- It does because these people need

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:41.000
to get structure back in their lives?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.352
Which I've me people here who probably

00:05:43.352 --> 00:05:46.830
haven't had to answer
to anyone in 10 years.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.089
- [Mark] I've heard from
several of the addicts

00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:51.160
who've had some success in
the past but then relapse now,

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.510
but they even said that the only way

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.510
that rehab is ever going to work

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.449
is if I just commit to
a full year or more.

00:05:56.449 --> 00:05:58.080
- Yeah, a full year. Yup, so our program,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.980
once they do the year they
can apply for a second year,

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.800
and then they can apply for a third year,

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.620
so our program isn't
due the year and then,

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.950
you know, great job, like people--

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.620
- [Mark] And this is, what
does it cost, or is it free?

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:09.453
- Free! All free of cost.

00:06:09.453 --> 00:06:11.160
First year, second year, third year,

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.030
so The Dream Center is a self-funded,

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.680
so it runs on donations.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:16.513
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:16.513 --> 00:06:19.760
- From other churches,
from people who donate

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.550
and things like that, but yeah.

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.220
I work in the program now,

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.600
so I do the first one to two weeks,

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.050
so when people coming in off the streets

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.580
and we have people coming in with

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.980
just the clothes that they're wearing

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.840
and they come in, you know,

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.470
they kind of have a week or two to detox

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:38.364
if they're coming off
alcohol, or crystal meth,

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.920
or heroin, or whatever.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.380
Some guys just come in because,
you know, divorce is common,

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.213
like things like that.

00:06:45.213 --> 00:06:48.130
So yeah, it's very common,

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.280
and then after the first two weeks

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:50.810
they move into an orientation phase,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.790
which is four weeks, and then
basically the first month is

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.524
like easing them into
it and then after that

00:06:55.524 --> 00:06:59.110
they start the real
phase which is level one,

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.570
which is three months, and
then level two, level three,

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.170
level four, and then they graduate, so.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:04.112
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:04.112 --> 00:07:05.370
- And then they get their
job around The Dream Center,

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.644
so you could be in the kitchen,
you could be construction.

00:07:07.644 --> 00:07:09.690
So it's giving them practical,

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.730
training them in how
to do practical stuff,

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:12.563
- [Mark] Something once they get out.

00:07:12.563 --> 00:07:13.440
- Keeping them busy, you know,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.960
it's actually teaching them a skill,

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.440
so once they do get
out of here, they said,

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.570
well for nine months I did
such and such, or yeah.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.740
- [Mark] I've seen so many comments

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.410
on some of the addiction videos.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.243
- Yeah.

00:07:23.243 --> 00:07:24.957
- [Mark] That I put on
my channel, that say,

00:07:24.957 --> 00:07:27.123
"well, why don't you just
walk this person over to rehab

00:07:27.123 --> 00:07:28.180
and get them all better,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.875
and everything will be
perfect after that."

00:07:29.875 --> 00:07:32.190
(Hayden laughing)

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.300
What would you say to that?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.391
- That's called leading
the horse to the water

00:07:35.391 --> 00:07:36.640
but you can't get it to drink.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.100
- [Mark] I heard somebody
that is in your line of work,

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.510
say, I thought this was a
great thing, they said that--

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:43.890
- Yeah.

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:46.790
- [Mark] If an addict wants
to quit, nobody can stop them.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.950
- Yeah.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.423
- [Mark] But if an addict
doesn't want to quit

00:07:49.423 --> 00:07:51.220
nobody can make them.
- Nobody can make them.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.650
- Yeah, exactly, and it's
like, guys will come in.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:55.680
I didn't do the interview with them,

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.210
but straight after the
interview they come in,

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.030
and then, so I'm like the
first point of contact

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.677
with some guys, and I'm like,

00:08:01.677 --> 00:08:03.052
"okay, so what brought you here?"

00:08:03.052 --> 00:08:05.190
And they're like "my
mom made me come here,"

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.090
and I say, straight away,

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.350
I'm like, "if your mom made you come here,

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:10.110
you're not gonna change,

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.570
and this program's
going to be lot harder."

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.550
Like, you have to want to be here.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.300
You can't come, you can't do rehab,

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.470
you can't get clean for
a spouse for, you know,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.160
I think it's a driving
motive, it can drive you,

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.440
but at the end, it's
not going to be enough,

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.890
'cause when it gets
tough and when it gets,

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:27.240
when things stop coming up,
that you haven't worked through,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.450
if you don't really want the
change, it's not going to work.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:30.760
Like you can do it for your children,

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.330
which I think is amazing,

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.720
but they really need to
change for themselves

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.170
to be better for the children.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:39.863
Not like so, as far as people wanting to,

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:41.880
yeah, I wish I could.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.170
Some days I almost want to come in

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.050
and abduct people in a van
and just bring them in.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.467
- [Mark] I know that's
almost like I talked a cop--

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:49.640
- And just come in the middle
of the night with a team.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.170
- [Mark] I spoke to a
police officer yesterday

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.160
about a 51 50.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.480
- Yeah. I've heard about that.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.860
- [Mark] 'Cause I've been talking with

00:08:55.781 --> 00:08:56.614
one of the guys I interviewed.

00:08:56.614 --> 00:08:57.447
His name is Paul.

00:08:57.447 --> 00:08:59.560
