00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.732
- [Mark] Yeah, well I
think helping others...

00:18:35.732 --> 00:18:36.565
- Perspective.

00:18:36.565 --> 00:18:37.398
- [Mark] Giving to others.

00:18:37.398 --> 00:18:39.113
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:42.060
- [Mark] Has some kind of
magical effect on a person.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.700
- Yeah, like our pastor, Matthew Barnett,

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.967
the pastor of The Dream
Center always says,

00:18:45.967 --> 00:18:47.920
"if you're in a rut or
you're feeling, you know,

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.370
depressed and down and he's
like go and serve others."

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.890
And it'll bring you, it's
not like a quick fit,

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:55.970
like meant to heal it, but
you'll just realize that

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:57.780
helping people who are in
a worse situation than you,

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.930
which is like what happened for me.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:01.067
The first time I came
down here, I was like,

00:19:01.067 --> 00:19:02.710
"whoa, my life's not that bad."

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:03.980
I lived in a house my whole life.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:07.150
I had two parents who
were awesome, you know.

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:11.090
I've got food, I've got
clothes, I've got this,

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:14.540
and you know, I met a dude
named, do you know Bart?

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:17.680
Young, white dude who
stays across from Whitney.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.960
He's always riding
around and riding a bike.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:19.831
He's got blonde hair.

00:19:19.831 --> 00:19:20.664
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:19:20.664 --> 00:19:21.497
- He was the first dude I met,

00:19:21.497 --> 00:19:22.330
and he's a year older than me.

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.820
And I was just like, "what
are you doing down here?"

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:26.650
And he was like, he
couldn't even answer it.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:27.640
I don't think anyone had asked him

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:29.142
what he was doing down
here, and he was like,

00:19:29.142 --> 00:19:31.990
"I don't know," and that just
blew me away, and I was like--

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:34.940
- [Mark] I think the tendency to be

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:40.531
a little like self
conscious, self obsessed--

00:19:40.531 --> 00:19:41.364
- Yeah.

00:19:41.364 --> 00:19:42.490
- [Mark] All that kind
of stuff, that a lot of,

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.963
you see in regular society all the time.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.740
Who's the comedian on
"Saturday Night Live"?

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:49.340
She does the Sarah Palin.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.210
- Oh, Tina Fey.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.100
- [Mark] Tina Fey, made a comment once,

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.160
I thought was great about this.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.030
- Yeah.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:56.900
- [Mark] And she says,

00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:00.140
Mother Teresa never worries
about her thighs touching.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:00.973
- Ah, yeah.

00:20:00.973 --> 00:20:01.806
- [Mark] You know, she's
always helping people.

00:20:01.806 --> 00:20:02.980
- Yeah, yeah.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:04.680
- [Mark] And she feels
great about herself,

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.660
regardless of how she's looking that day

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:09.093
or how her skin or hair or whatever looks,

00:20:09.948 --> 00:20:12.220
and I think there's a
lot of truth in that.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:13.240
- Yeah, definitely.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:16.070
Like, I think you come
in here and you realize

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:18.240
how much you actually
do have without knowing,

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:23.240
like, it's almost like,
it really threw me off,

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.390
'cause I was like, wow.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.560
I just feel like a real
sense of conviction

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:28.410
of feeling ungrateful for my life.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.800
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:31.940
- And this is like Skid
Row, and then, you know,

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:35.150
I haven't been to third world
countries, but this is...

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.350
- [Mark] I mean, gratitude
is a hard thing to just,

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.183
you know, everybody says,

00:20:38.183 --> 00:20:39.016
"Oh, we should have our gratitude."

00:20:39.016 --> 00:20:39.849
- Yeah.

00:20:39.849 --> 00:20:41.660
- [Mark] That sounds good on paper,

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:43.157
but how do you actually do it?

00:20:43.157 --> 00:20:43.990
- Yeah.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.620
- [Mark] And I found by, you know,

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:46.658
I believe I'm helping somebody.

00:20:46.658 --> 00:20:47.517
- Yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:20:47.517 --> 00:20:48.649
- [Mark] And I've heard
it a thousand times,

00:20:48.649 --> 00:20:50.050
but I also heard that
I'm exploiting people

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:51.380
and all this other
stuff, which I don't buy,

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:53.210
but there's some truth in that.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:54.043
- Yeah.

00:20:54.043 --> 00:20:54.876
- [Mark] You know, when...

00:20:55.744 --> 00:20:56.577
(Mark sighs)

00:20:56.577 --> 00:20:58.120
How do you, I mean,
what's the best analogy.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.070
When a wealthy man...

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:04.147
When an attractive female
marries a wealthy man

00:21:04.147 --> 00:21:07.610
is she doing it because of
this security he'll provide,

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.840
or is it because it's true love?

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:09.710
- Yeah.

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:10.829
- [Mark] There's probably
a little bit of both.

00:21:10.829 --> 00:21:11.662
- A bit of both, yeah.

00:21:11.662 --> 00:21:13.860
- [Mark] And when a man buys
an expensive sports car,

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:15.730
is it because he
appreciates fine automobiles

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:16.947
or is it because he feels insecure?

00:21:16.947 --> 00:21:17.780
- Yeah.

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:18.613
- [Mark] It's a little bit of both.

00:21:18.613 --> 00:21:19.800
It's always a little bit of both.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.100
And so am I exploiting people?

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:22.550
Yes, of course I'm exploiting people,

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:26.180
but every single person I
didn't coerce, or trick,

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.007
or manipulate them into coming in.

00:21:28.007 --> 00:21:28.840
- Yeah.

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:30.030
- [Mark] I said, would
you like to do this?

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:31.800
And very often I even forget to mention

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:32.750
that there's money involved.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:33.583
- Yeah.

00:21:33.583 --> 00:21:34.416
- [Mark] And then they
find out that there is,

00:21:34.416 --> 00:21:35.638
and, "Oh, that's great. I didn't
realize we would get paid."

00:21:35.638 --> 00:21:36.812
- Yeah.

00:21:36.812 --> 00:21:39.210
- [Mark] And so on the one hand, yes,

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.700
I'm sure if you look at it
negatively I'm exploiting them,

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:42.533
- Yeah.

00:21:42.533 --> 00:21:43.570
- [Mark] But in a positive light

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:46.230
I think I'm helping them to unload a lot

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.500
of their hidden closeted garbage that...

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.660
- Yeah, it just unravels, yeah.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.280
- [Mark] They're wearing it
every day of their lives.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:56.580
And I've heard from several
people that I've talked to

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.950
that said they've stopped using

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:01.360
since they had to talk in front of me.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:02.193
- That's amazing.

00:22:02.193 --> 00:22:03.026
- [Mark] So that's interesting,

00:22:03.026 --> 00:22:04.590
but I'm not saying I'm healing anything.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.140
I think just unloading their...

00:22:06.982 --> 00:22:08.520
- It's always like as much as you want,

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:10.170
I think like as much as
you want someone to hear,

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:12.230
you know, what's your story.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:15.230
You don't think these
people want, you know,

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:17.790
people to know their story and
know how their day is going.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:20.380
I think it's just like,
that's where, 'cause I know

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:22.320
we don't have a lot of
homeless people in Australia.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.190
And then, so my mindset was
kind of stereotype based

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:26.460
when I came here and then I just realized,

00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:28.890
and I was like, they're just people.

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:31.723
Flesh, bone, you know, they're human.

00:22:31.723 --> 00:22:33.310
They're exactly the same as me.

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:35.355
They check out, and it's just like,

00:22:35.355 --> 00:22:39.130
you know, they have feelings.
I'm sure they know that,

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:42.040
yeah, they're here, and
just hearing that, yeah.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:44.980
I would just encourage, like
go talk to a homeless person.

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.570
Go find their story and
find what they need.

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:51.473
Just give you a good sense of, yeah,

00:22:52.463 --> 00:22:54.140
where you're at and what you have,

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:57.130
and then you'd probably
cherish it a little bit more

00:22:57.130 --> 00:23:01.500
and walk around with a little
more sense of gratitude,

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:02.333
I'd say.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.430
- [Mark] Yeah, I've never been happier

00:23:04.430 --> 00:23:06.053
since I started doing this.

00:23:06.053 --> 00:23:08.373
- Yeah. This like, healed my...

00:23:08.373 --> 00:23:09.206
You know, because I'm helping people,

00:23:09.206 --> 00:23:11.730
because I just realized that,
hey, my life's pretty good,

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:13.633
and like depression.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.010
I can be in the worst mood

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:18.390
and I come down here and I'm like, wow.

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:19.810
- [Mark] Yeah, it's not so much

00:23:19.810 --> 00:23:22.800
that I'm comparing my life to
their poor miserable lives,

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:25.410
but there's something about what I'm doing

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:28.020
that makes me feel better about myself

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:31.474
and that bleeds into
every aspect of my life.

00:23:31.474 --> 00:23:33.000
- Yeah.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:34.920
- [Mark] From the way
I sleep to everything.

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:35.840
- Yeah, yeah.

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:36.720
- [Mark] You just stand up straighter,

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:37.730
you feel better about yourself.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:38.650
- Yeah, you can go to bed knowing that,

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:40.340
hey, I kind of helped.

00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:42.710
I did something today that
helped someone, you know?

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:43.979
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:23:43.979 --> 00:23:44.812
- Yeah, I didn't just--

00:23:44.812 --> 00:23:47.176
- [Mark] Yeah, I've had countless people.

00:23:47.176 --> 00:23:49.351
I've talked to, I think 1300 people now.

00:23:49.351 --> 00:23:51.320
- Wow. 1300, wow.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:52.922
- [Mark] And I can't count
how many people have come back

00:23:52.922 --> 00:23:53.870
and said, "Oh my God, that was so great.

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:54.960
I want to do that again."

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:55.793
- Wow.

00:23:55.793 --> 00:23:56.626
- [Mark] They almost all do that.

00:23:56.626 --> 00:23:57.459
- Yeah.

00:23:57.459 --> 00:23:58.572
- [Mark] Almost everybody I speak to,

00:23:58.572 --> 00:23:59.530
if I see them again, like "can
I do that again?" (chuckles)

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:00.363
- That's amazing.

00:24:00.363 --> 00:24:01.590
- [Mark] And it's like,

00:24:01.590 --> 00:24:03.132
so I think there's something
very therapeutic about...

00:24:03.132 --> 00:24:05.020
- Yeah, definitely, yeah.

00:24:05.020 --> 00:24:07.550
- [Mark] Getting your stuff
out in the light of day

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:10.840
letting everybody hear it, at
least in theory, on YouTube

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:13.520
you're talking to the entire
planet, in theory. Right?

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:14.353
- Yeah.

00:24:14.353 --> 00:24:15.760
- [Mark] And there's something
very powerful in that.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:17.017
- Definitely, yeah.

00:24:17.017 --> 00:24:19.330
- [Mark] And it frees you up to it to...

00:24:21.070 --> 00:24:25.100
It keeps you from being
locked into doing the same

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.260
defensive mechanism behaviors
that you've always done.

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:28.093
- Yeah.

00:24:28.093 --> 00:24:30.970
- [Mark] And you're free to do
otherwise, if you choose to.

00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:32.430
It just takes a little
bit of courage to do that.

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:35.630
- Yeah, it does, yeah. It
does take a big of courage

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:37.979
to go walk up to, 'cause
I remember I was scared

00:24:37.979 --> 00:24:38.870
of homeless people as a kid.

00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:41.850
We went to New York City
once, and you know--

00:24:41.850 --> 00:24:43.020
- [Mark] Well, I'm not saying, no,

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:44.240
courage is not an issue for me,

00:24:44.240 --> 00:24:47.090
but courage for them
to unload these things.

00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:48.014
- Oh, yeah, yeah, sorry.

00:24:48.014 --> 00:24:48.847
- [Mark] That's what I'm talking about.

00:24:48.847 --> 00:24:49.680
- Yeah, definitely.

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:51.220
- [Mark] I mean, it takes a lot
of courage for these people.

00:24:51.220 --> 00:24:53.307
- Yeah, because you'll
get people who will ask,

00:24:53.307 --> 00:24:54.910
"Hey, what's your story?" and I see it.

00:24:54.910 --> 00:24:58.100
And I can see the, you can
say them trying to process it

00:24:58.100 --> 00:24:59.580
of like, oh no I can't bring that up

00:24:59.580 --> 00:25:03.850
or I don't trust this
person and then, you know,

00:25:03.850 --> 00:25:05.170
I might be times where I've come down

00:25:05.170 --> 00:25:07.398
and then it might be the
fourth time that person

00:25:07.398 --> 00:25:11.170
finally opens up, and then
we're able to actually be like,

00:25:11.170 --> 00:25:13.507
okay, you know, now we can help.

00:25:13.507 --> 00:25:16.390
What do you need? You need
shoes or you need this?

00:25:16.390 --> 00:25:18.200
We have the program we have, you know,

00:25:18.200 --> 00:25:20.630
it's just until they yeah, you know.

00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:23.543
Until they open up and they
want the help it's kind of,

00:25:23.543 --> 00:25:25.280
it's the same with addiction

00:25:25.280 --> 00:25:28.310
or whether I need services or whatever.

00:25:28.310 --> 00:25:30.688
- [Mark] Yeah, I think what
The Dream Center is providing

00:25:30.688 --> 00:25:34.750
is, it's what every
person down here needs,

00:25:34.750 --> 00:25:36.430
but they also have to want it.

00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:38.153
- [Hayden] Yeah, they
have to want it, yeah.

00:25:39.400 --> 00:25:40.233
- [Mark] All right, Hayden,

00:25:40.233 --> 00:25:41.195
well, thank you so much for talking to me.

00:25:41.195 --> 00:25:42.028
- [Hayden] Thank you.

00:25:42.028 --> 00:25:43.400
- [Mark] And good luck with
everything you're doing.

00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:44.233
I'm proud of you.

00:25:44.233 --> 00:25:45.410
- [Hayden] Yeah, thank you man.

00:25:45.410 --> 00:25:46.243
The world needs more people like you.

00:25:46.243 --> 00:25:47.443
- Thank you, thank you very much.

00:25:47.443 --> 00:25:49.230
- [Mark] All right, thank you.

00:25:49.230 --> 00:25:50.063
- [Hayden] Wow.

00:25:51.460 --> 00:25:52.293
- [Mark] That was cool.

00:25:52.293 --> 00:25:53.126
- [Hayden] Yeah.

00:25:53.126 --> 00:25:53.959
- [Mark] And you're wearing
the right color shirt

00:25:53.959 --> 00:25:54.792
for my background.

00:25:54.792 --> 00:25:55.719
- [Hayden] Oh, yeah!

00:25:55.719 --> 00:25:56.610
- [Mark] (laughing) It was perfect.

00:25:56.610 --> 00:25:57.542
Couldn't have done better.

00:25:57.542 --> 00:25:58.488
- [Hayden] I don't have many shirts,

00:25:58.488 --> 00:26:00.238
half my wardrobe is...

